["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ark", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Archival Resource Key (ARK)](https://arks.org/about/), is a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) suited to being a persistent identifier for information objects of any type, standardized by the [ARK Identifier Scheme](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-kunze-ark/) Internet-Draft. It consists of the \"ark:\" label followed by a Name Assigning Authority Number, a forward slash, a name, and an optional qualifier (e.g., `ark:12148/btv1b8449691v/f29`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasOutput", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `from` Element generates each `to` Element as an output.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nfd6084385d03463d84fd5d45527abd96", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/implementedBy", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/doi", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Digital Object Identifier (DOI)](https://www.doi.org/the-identifier/what-is-a-doi/) is a unique, [ISO 26324](https://www.iso.org/standard/88862.html)-standardized identifier for physical, digital, or abstract objects, formatted as a prefix and suffix separated by a forward slash (e.g., `10.1000/182`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/BoundaryDefinitionAction", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The boundary definition is used to define boundaries.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N4d5053a06bc84ab69504bd5f65df6449", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N2f259676c4614e3b9b9292d97a04a294", "localId", "", ""]
["_:Nb7a5cf0c2a384fa59053e068ddf9abe4", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message", "When relationship is fixedBy, to must be an Agent", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iswc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Musical Work Code (ISWC)](https://www.iswc.org/iswc) is an 11-character unique identifier standardized by [ISO 15707](https://www.iso.org/standard/83125.html) for musical works (compositions) as distinct from specific recordings. While the \"ISWC\" label and grouping separators (dots and hyphens) are used for human readability, they shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `T0017812031`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/AnnotationType/review", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/AnnotationType", "globalId", "", ""]
